--- body ---
## Context

Upstream advanced two releases past the reviewed baseline on 2026-08-31:
`UPSTREAM` declares v1.10.0 (`b132f2d`, reviewed 2026-08-29), upstream `main` is
now v1.12.0 (`b05ed69`), with v1.11.0 (`ee50cea`) between them.
`make upstream-status` reports STALE.

This is not a formatting change. `git diff --stat v1.10.0..main -- src/features/search/`
is +1738/-57 across ten files, three of them new (`own-words-source.ts`,
`vector-salvage.ts`, `electron.ts`). `spec/README.md`'s standing -- 23 rows on two
axes plus an evidence column -- was read against v1.10.0 source, and a judgement
about that release is not evidence about this one.

The guard already knows. `bench/check_progress.py` `check_baseline()` is
default-deny: the page may name the release `UPSTREAM` declares reviewed and no
other. Its own words: "when the baseline moves the honest act is to invalidate
the page rather than to let it keep answering for a release it never saw." So
`make check` goes red the moment `UPSTREAM` is bumped, and stays red until every
row has been read again. That is the design, not an obstacle to route around.

Split from the 2026-08-31 reconciliation pass (SYNC.md, tickets) deliberately:
recording what upstream did is cheap and was done immediately; re-reading the
standing is author-gated. Ten of the twenty-three verdicts carry
`evidence: measured`, and they rest on `bench/results/smoke-1.10.0/checks.json`,
produced by `bench/smoke_upstream.py` driven against the author's real Zotero
library. That library is not in this repo and no agent session can reach it.
Bumping the baseline without re-running it would silently demote ten `measured`
rows to `inferred` -- the exact dishonesty the evidence column was split to
prevent.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `UPSTREAM` names v1.12.0 / `b05ed69a88e3a0c1ef874f57f97a0e11ddf7ec3c`, with the review date
- [ ] Every one of the 23 rows in `spec/README.md` re-read against v1.12.0 source, both axes and the evidence word
- [ ] The four version mentions in `spec/README.md` (lines 33, 239, 271, 278 at the time of filing) name v1.12.0 and no other release
- [ ] `bench/smoke_upstream.py` re-run against v1.12.0 on the author's machine, its artifact committed under `bench/results/`
- [ ] Any figure the re-measurement moves is updated at every prose site `bench/check_figures.py` names
- [ ] `make check` green and `make upstream-status` green together
